\[
\text{Volume} = \text{Length} \times \text{Width} \times \text{Depth}
\]
Substitute the given dimensions:
\[
\text{Volume} = 25 \, \text{ft} \times 14 \, \text{ft} \times 4 \, \text{ft} = 1400 \, \text{cubic feet}
\]

### Step 2: Convert the volume to gallons.
The problem states that the number of gallons is calculated by multiplying the volume by 5.9:
\[
\text{Gallons} = \text{Volume} \times 5.9
\]
Substitute the volume:
\[
\text{Gallons} = 1400 \times 5.9 = 8260 \, \text{gallons}
\]

### Step 3: Calculate the cost to fill the pool.
The cost is $0.10 per gallon. Multiply the number of gallons by the cost per gallon:
\[
\text{Cost} = \text{Gallons} \times \text{Cost per gallon}
\]
Substitute the values:
\[
